// AN EFFECT OP IS A FUNCTION VALUE, or it refuses — never both compiling
// clean and dying at the assembler. The op face of
// Hβ.emit.nonfn-binding-as-function-value, born RED 2026-09-09: `each(note,
// xs)` checked with ZERO diagnostics and emitted `(global.get $note)` for a
// global that never existed, so wat2wasm objected about a symbol hundreds of
// thousands of lines from anything the developer wrote.
//
// A bare op name is the parameter product with every field a hole, so it
// reifies through the same partial mint a constructor does — with one law
// the constructor does not need: the dispatch tier must be the SINGLETON
// one. The lexical tier names a state local of the frame the reification
// site is in, and the synthesized body is a LIFTED fn where that frame is
// gone; the world-chain resolve inside the body reads the handler that is
// installed when the closure is actually CALLED, which is the only handler
// the escaped value can honestly mean.
//
// The performs must really land, so the answer is read back through the
// handler's own state: 1 + 2 + 3. Expected: 6.
effect Log {
  note(n: Int)
  total() -> Int
}

handler counter with sum = 0 {
  note(n) => resume() with sum = sum + n,
  total() => resume(sum),
}

fn tally() = {
  each(note, [1, 2, 3])
  total()
} ~> counter

fn main() = tally()
